  "prefLabel": "Dec 204.04 Motions",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 204.04 Motions.\n\n(a) A motion may be filed at any time by a party to a proceeding or by a person who has filed a motion to intervene which has not been denied.\n\n(b) All motions shall be filed in writing.\n\n(c) A motion shall clearly and concisely state:\n\n(1) The facts and law that support the motion and the specific relief or ruling requested; and\n\n(2) Certification that the party has made a good faith attempt to obtain the concurrence of the other parties in the relief sought.\n\n(d) Objections to a motion, except for motions for rehearing, shall be in writing and filed within 10 days of the date on which the motion is filed, unless otherwise ordered.\n\n(e) Objections to a motion for rehearing pursuant to RSA 541:3 shall be filed within 3 days of the date on which the motion for rehearing is filed.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A eff 4-25-08",
